# Pages & routing (`src/pages/**`)

- **Default chrome:** Most marketing/content pages should use **`BaseLayout`** (`src/layouts/BaseLayout.astro`) unless a specialized layout already wraps content (`BlogLayout`, `GalleryLayout`, `StoreLayout`, `TeamLayout`, `LegalLayout`).
- **Detail routes** use **`[...slug].astro`** with `getStaticPaths` mapping **`params.slug` to `entry.id`** from the content collection (`posts`, `store`, `team`, `gallery`, `legal`).
- **Canonical URL patterns** (how cards link today):
  - Blog posts: `/blog/posts/{id}`
  - Tags: `/blog/tags` and `/blog/tags/{tag}`
  - Store: `/store/{id}`
  - Gallery: `/gallery/posts/{id}`
  - Team: `/team/{id}`
  - Legal: `/legal/{id}` (source files under `src/content/infopages/`)
- **RSS:** `src/pages/rss.xml.js` — item links use `/blog/posts/${post.id}/` and `context.site` from `astro.config.mjs`.
- **System routes** (`src/pages/system/*`) are Lexington UI reference pages; keep them behind the existing structure when adding demos.
- Prefer **`@/` imports** in new pages to match the rest of the codebase.
